\newlabel{fig:s4_state_marginals}{{6}{28}{Per-component marginals of the true mechanical state $\mathbf {s}_t$ (blue) and the phantom state $\tilde {\mathbf {s}}_t$ (orange), TurboSens2 train split. Efficiency channels at even indices overlap almost perfectly; flow capacity channels at odd indices are displaced upward in $\tilde {\mathbf {s}}_t$ by the fouling-driven coupling $C\mathbf {c}_t$. The gap between the two histograms is exactly the non-identifiability signal the world model must learn to close by integrating the action history.\relax }{figure.caption.74}{}}
