\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces TurboSens1 hidden state trajectories under the four degradation archetypes (A compressor, B fan/booster, C turbine, D balanced). Each panel overlays the ten state components for a single representative episode; vertical green and orange lines mark maintenance interventions. Archetype D produces nearly flat trajectories that survive the full $10{,}000$ step horizon without intervention, while A and C show the steeper early drift that drives recurring maintenance.\relax }}{36}{figure.caption.94}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gallery_s3_archetypes}{{13}{36}{TurboSens1 hidden state trajectories under the four degradation archetypes (A compressor, B fan/booster, C turbine, D balanced). Each panel overlays the ten state components for a single representative episode; vertical green and orange lines mark maintenance interventions. Archetype D produces nearly flat trajectories that survive the full $10{,}000$ step horizon without intervention, while A and C show the steeper early drift that drives recurring maintenance.\relax }{figure.caption.94}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces Single TurboSens1 episode (archetype C, observed under the \texttt  {CR\_nominal} flight context). Top: the ten dimensional hidden state $\mathbf  {s}_t$ evolving as a sawtooth of partial resets. Middle: the seven dimensional sensor stream $\mathbf  {o}_t$ at the chosen context, showing how observation noise and contextual variation obscure the underlying state. Bottom: the discrete maintenance action sequence; coloured markers indicate the action type at each maintenance event.\relax }}{37}{figure.caption.95}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gallery_s3_episode}{{14}{37}{Single TurboSens1 episode (archetype C, observed under the \texttt {CR\_nominal} flight context). Top: the ten dimensional hidden state $\mathbf {s}_t$ evolving as a sawtooth of partial resets. Middle: the seven dimensional sensor stream $\mathbf {o}_t$ at the chosen context, showing how observation noise and contextual variation obscure the underlying state. Bottom: the discrete maintenance action sequence; coloured markers indicate the action type at each maintenance event.\relax }{figure.caption.95}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces Weather process for a single TurboSens1 episode: the ambient temperature deviation $\Delta T_\mathrm  {amb}$ follows a slow Ornstein-Uhlenbeck trajectory (top) and rain events (bottom) are gated by the seasonal phase, here at a $22.7\%$ episode wide rain rate.\relax }}{37}{figure.caption.96}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gallery_s3_weather}{{15}{37}{Weather process for a single TurboSens1 episode: the ambient temperature deviation $\Delta T_\mathrm {amb}$ follows a slow Ornstein-Uhlenbeck trajectory (top) and rain events (bottom) are gated by the seasonal phase, here at a $22.7\%$ episode wide rain rate.\relax }{figure.caption.96}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces TurboSens1 sensor / state correlation matrix. Context averaged Pearson correlations between the seven sensor channels and the ten hidden state dimensions, computed over the train split. Most cells are near zero, but a handful of strong positive (HP shaft speed vs HPC efficiency / flow, $r \in [0.5, 0.6]$) and strong negative (LP shaft speed vs HPC flow, $r = -0.76$) couplings establish that the observation map is informative about the latent state but far from a one-to-one decoder; this is the structure the inverse evaluation protocol asks the encoder to recover.\relax }}{38}{figure.caption.97}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gallery_s3_sensor_state_corr}{{16}{38}{TurboSens1 sensor / state correlation matrix. Context averaged Pearson correlations between the seven sensor channels and the ten hidden state dimensions, computed over the train split. Most cells are near zero, but a handful of strong positive (HP shaft speed vs HPC efficiency / flow, $r \in [0.5, 0.6]$) and strong negative (LP shaft speed vs HPC flow, $r = -0.76$) couplings establish that the observation map is informative about the latent state but far from a one-to-one decoder; this is the structure the inverse evaluation protocol asks the encoder to recover.\relax }{figure.caption.97}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {17}{\ignorespaces TurboSens2 per region sensor distributions, pooled over all timesteps and contexts. Each panel shows a box plot of one of the seven sensor channels across the six geographic regions (Arid, Littoral, Continental, Equatorial, Highland, Industrial). Region affects both the median and the spread of every channel, most noticeably on HPC inlet and outlet temperatures (HPC\_Tin, HPC\_Tout) where the Highland and Arid extremes are visibly separated. The OOD evaluation in Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:ood} relies on held out region / archetype draws sitting in these distributional tails.\relax }}{38}{figure.caption.98}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gallery_s4_regions}{{17}{38}{TurboSens2 per region sensor distributions, pooled over all timesteps and contexts. Each panel shows a box plot of one of the seven sensor channels across the six geographic regions (Arid, Littoral, Continental, Equatorial, Highland, Industrial). Region affects both the median and the spread of every channel, most noticeably on HPC inlet and outlet temperatures (HPC\_Tin, HPC\_Tout) where the Highland and Arid extremes are visibly separated. The OOD evaluation in Section~\ref {sec:ood} relies on held out region / archetype draws sitting in these distributional tails.\relax }{figure.caption.98}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {18}{\ignorespaces Full trajectory of a TurboSens2 episode in the Arid region (archetype C, $T \approx 8000$ steps, $\sim 100$ engine washes, $5$ shop visits). Each row shows one of the seven sensors over the full episode. Vertical red and orange markers indicate shop visits and engine washes respectively; the dramatic dips in HP\_Nmech and HPC\_Pout\_st around the shop visits are visible directly in the sensor stream. The bottom two rows show the calendar month and a fouling proxy, illustrating how often the wash action is exercised in a high fouling region.\relax }}{39}{figure.caption.99}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gallery_s4_trajectory_arid}{{18}{39}{Full trajectory of a TurboSens2 episode in the Arid region (archetype C, $T \approx 8000$ steps, $\sim 100$ engine washes, $5$ shop visits). Each row shows one of the seven sensors over the full episode. Vertical red and orange markers indicate shop visits and engine washes respectively; the dramatic dips in HP\_Nmech and HPC\_Pout\_st around the shop visits are visible directly in the sensor stream. The bottom two rows show the calendar month and a fouling proxy, illustrating how often the wash action is exercised in a high fouling region.\relax }{figure.caption.99}{}}
